@@ -3,6 +3,13 @@
 The web tier drops one raw export per UTC day into data/pageviews/<YYYY-MM-DD>.csv
 at about 01:00 UTC the next morning. This DAG aggregates yesterday's file into
 the `daily_pageviews` table (views and unique visitors per page).
+
+Each run loads the UTC day that its data interval starts on. With the 03:00
+schedule the run at D+1 03:00 covers interval [D 03:00, D+1 03:00) and loads
+day D, i.e. "yesterday" once the 01:00 export has landed. Data begins on
+2026-09-01, so that is the start_date; catchup backfills every day since.
+Re-running a day replaces that day's rows (delete + insert in one transaction),
+so it never double counts.
 """
 
